149
00:13:28.207 --> 00:13:33.170
♪ Wind shall blow for evermore ♪

150
00:13:34.878 --> 00:13:36.046
Robin!

151
00:13:37.846 --> 00:13:39.097
Robin!

152
00:13:40.749 --> 00:13:43.086
Bread? (LAUGHS)

153
00:13:45.061 --> 00:13:46.479
This is a good adventure.

154
00:13:48.358 --> 00:13:49.608
A good adventure.

155
00:13:52.905 --> 00:13:55.925
You remember
when we met the potter.

156
00:13:55.949 --> 00:13:59.012
did we leave him naked
or did we kill him?

157
00:13:59.036 --> 00:14:00.889
Oh. I tried to tell the story

158
00:14:00.913 --> 00:14:03.040
and someone said
we left him naked.

159
00:14:03.444 --> 00:14:04.821
But I couldn't remember.

160
00:14:05.793 --> 00:14:07.985
You always told it well. Robin.

161
00:14:09.755 --> 00:14:11.613
Why would we leave him naked?

162
00:14:12.863 --> 00:14:14.072
I don't know.

163
00:14:15.969 --> 00:14:17.387
It were a jest.

164
00:14:18.722 --> 00:14:20.015
We never met a potter.

165
00:14:20.773 --> 00:14:22.709
What do you mean
we never met him?

166
00:14:22.734 --> 00:14:23.920
ROBIN: I mean.
that never happened.

167
00:14:23.944 --> 00:14:26.444
It's just a story
you heard somewhere.

168
00:14:27.498 --> 00:14:28.643
(SCOFFS)

169
00:14:28.668 --> 00:14:30.325
ROBIN: But if we did meet
a potter.

170
00:14:31.359 --> 00:14:32.712
we killed him.

171
00:14:32.736 --> 00:14:34.630
I'd remember if it were a story.

172
00:14:34.655 --> 00:14:36.615
(GRUNTS) Here!

173
00:14:37.074 --> 00:14:38.491
Tell me about your wife.

174
00:14:41.411 --> 00:14:42.495
Margaret.

175
00:14:44.581 --> 00:14:46.392
She's a good woman.

176
00:14:46.416 --> 00:14:50.146
She's a very good woman.
She's pious.

177
00:14:50.170 --> 00:14:52.065
She teaches me prayerfulness.

178
00:14:52.089 --> 00:14:53.340
Paint a portrait.

179
00:14:55.175 --> 00:14:56.468
Paint a portrait?

180
00:14:57.928 --> 00:15:00.513
(CHUCKLES) Paint a portrait?

181
00:15:05.018 --> 00:15:09.564
She has hair that's red.

182
00:15:10.232 --> 00:15:11.835
ROBIN: Red like?

183
00:15:11.859 --> 00:15:14.045
Red like fresh blood.

184
00:15:14.069 --> 00:15:16.214
ROBIN: No. not blood.
No. no. no.

185
00:15:16.238 --> 00:15:19.074
Something that's red
and that's good. like her.

186
00:15:20.158 --> 00:15:21.785
Red like... I don't know.

187
00:15:25.873 --> 00:15:27.308
Like the setting sun.

188
00:15:27.332 --> 00:15:31.044
Aye. like
the setting summer sun.

189
00:15:32.420 --> 00:15:34.858
Margaret's a good wife.

190
00:15:34.882 --> 00:15:38.051
With hair that's red
like the setting summer sun.

191
00:15:39.928 --> 00:15:41.221
She cares for me.

192
00:15:42.317 --> 00:15:43.766
And I care for her.

193
00:15:46.470 --> 00:15:48.056
(GRUNTS SOFTLY)

194
00:15:48.736 --> 00:15:49.736
ROBIN: Hmm.

195
00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:56.156
EDWARD: Robin. there are open
lands past the mountains.

196
00:15:58.298 --> 00:16:00.091
Many places to begin again.

197
00:16:05.089 --> 00:16:07.133
No. I do not aim to begin again.

198
00:16:12.606 --> 00:16:14.232
I aim for a right death.

199
00:16:16.761 --> 00:16:18.864
(DOG BARKING)

200
00:16:18.889 --> 00:16:21.141
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

201
00:16:40.262 --> 00:16:42.890
(WIND BLOWING)

202
00:17:02.102 --> 00:17:04.312
(TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES PLAYING)

203
00:17:12.582 --> 00:17:14.668
-(MAN YELLS. GROANS)
-(KNIFE SLASHING)

204
00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:19.602
(GAGGING AND GASPING)

205
00:17:38.291 --> 00:17:40.459
(TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES PLAYING)

206
00:17:55.567 --> 00:17:57.208
-(EDWARD GRUNTS)
-MARGARET: Edward!

207
00:17:57.232 --> 00:17:58.334
HENDRIE'S FATHER: Go. Hendrie!

208
00:17:58.358 --> 00:18:00.086
MARGARET: Edward!

209
00:18:00.110 --> 00:18:02.487
Go. Hendrie. run! Now!

210
00:18:02.512 --> 00:18:04.240
-Edward!
-Back!

211
00:18:04.265 --> 00:18:06.784
-(HENDRIE PANTING)
-Hendrie. get the others!

212
00:18:06.809 --> 00:18:08.491
MARGARET: Edward!

213
00:18:09.516 --> 00:18:12.185
(PANTING) Edward. my love...

214
00:18:13.228 --> 00:18:15.080
Watch over Little Margaret.

215
00:18:15.165 --> 00:18:16.643
-(MAN YELLS)
-(MARGARET SCREAMS)

216
00:18:16.668 --> 00:18:18.712
(SCREAMING)

217
00:18:20.106 --> 00:18:22.149
(EDWARD AND MAN GRUNTING)

218
00:18:27.197 --> 00:18:29.367
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

219
00:18:30.818 --> 00:18:32.360
(PANTING)

220
00:18:33.775 --> 00:18:35.151
(CRYING)

221
00:18:38.418 --> 00:18:39.419
(GRUNTS)

222
00:18:53.043 --> 00:18:55.254
(MUFFLED POUNDING)

223
00:18:59.253 --> 00:19:00.714
(EDWARD GRUNTING)

224
00:19:05.577 --> 00:19:08.080
(YELLING MANIACALLY)

225
00:19:09.296 --> 00:19:11.131
(BREATHING RAGGEDLY)

226
00:19:15.149 --> 00:19:16.900
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

227
00:19:24.897 --> 00:19:26.899
(EDWARD CRYING SOFTLY)

228
00:19:37.287 --> 00:19:38.831
(SNIFFLES AND GURGLES)

229
00:19:42.263 --> 00:19:44.098
(SOBBING)

230
00:19:51.820 --> 00:19:54.281
(EDWARD SCREAMS)

231
00:19:56.815 --> 00:19:59.026
(CONTINUES SOBBING)

232
00:20:00.264 --> 00:20:01.766
(LITTLE MARGARET WHIMPERS)

233
00:20:09.743 --> 00:20:12.973
Little one. don't worry.

234
00:20:12.998 --> 00:20:16.685
Don't worry.
Come here. come here.

235
00:20:16.721 --> 00:20:19.349
You're safe.
You're safe. daughter.

236
00:20:23.297 --> 00:20:25.549
Let us pray. Let us pray.

237
00:20:27.847 --> 00:20:30.826
O Lord. our God.

238
00:20:30.851 --> 00:20:34.688
grant us grace to desire Thee
with our whole heart.

239
00:20:35.226 --> 00:20:37.287
Come on now. pray.

240
00:20:37.312 --> 00:20:40.458
BOTH: And in finding Thee.
we may love Thee.

241
00:20:40.483 --> 00:20:43.420
And in loving Thee.
we may hate those sins

242
00:20:43.445 --> 00:20:46.132
from which Thou hast
redeemed us.

243
00:20:46.157 --> 00:20:49.202
For the sake of Jesus Christ.
Amen.

244
00:20:51.265 --> 00:20:54.328
Yes. Yes. good.

245
00:20:54.353 --> 00:20:57.272
Good. (SOBS. GRUNTS)

246
00:21:08.996 --> 00:21:10.248
(SHEEP BLEATING)

247
00:21:59.182 --> 00:22:00.183
(BREATHES HEAVILY)

248
00:22:03.505 --> 00:22:04.785
HENDRIE: (WHISPERING) I'm sorry.

249
00:22:05.886 --> 00:22:07.161
I'm sorry.

250
00:22:10.292 --> 00:22:11.535
I'm sorry.

251
00:22:12.860 --> 00:22:15.112
It were that when I woke.

252
00:22:17.456 --> 00:22:19.083
It were that when I woke.

253
00:22:20.354 --> 00:22:21.916
SHEPHERD: Cousin.

254
00:22:21.941 --> 00:22:23.943
It were that when I woke.

255
00:22:25.002 --> 00:22:26.420
I'm sorry.

256
00:22:28.403 --> 00:22:33.509
TRAVELER: ♪ The wind
between the north and east ♪

257
00:22:33.546 --> 00:22:37.134
♪ Blowed every chill and cold ♪

258
00:22:38.883 --> 00:22:43.446
♪ Or coldly blowed to me.
at least ♪

259
00:22:43.471 --> 00:22:46.934
♪ My clothes were thin and old ♪

260
00:22:47.915 --> 00:22:52.604
♪ The grass all dropping wet
with dew ♪

261
00:22:52.629 --> 00:22:55.382
♪ Low bent their tiny spears ♪

262
