♪ The lowly daisy bended too ♪

263
00:23:01.817 --> 00:23:06.571
♪ More lowly with my tears ♪

264
00:23:08.760 --> 00:23:13.848
♪ Oh. luckless youth
to sorrow born ♪

265
00:23:14.585 --> 00:23:17.295
♪ Shun'd son of poverty ♪

266
00:23:18.915 --> 00:23:23.502
♪ The world made gamely
sport and scorn ♪

267
00:23:24.358 --> 00:23:27.024
♪ And grinning infamy ♪

268
00:23:28.109 --> 00:23:32.172
♪ Unequalled though
my sorrow seems ♪

269
00:23:32.197 --> 00:23:35.636
♪ But great indeed they are ♪

270
00:23:35.661 --> 00:23:39.539
♪ Oh hear my sorrows
for my stream ♪

271
00:23:40.596 --> 00:23:44.809
♪ You'll find an equal there ♪

272
00:23:46.493 --> 00:23:50.470
♪ The land and Eddings
are no more ♪

273
00:23:51.147 --> 00:23:54.108
♪ The pastures too are gone ♪

274
00:23:56.056 --> 00:24:00.758
♪ The greens. the meadows
and the moors ♪

275
00:24:00.783 --> 00:24:03.469
♪ Are all cut up and gone ♪

276
00:24:03.494 --> 00:24:05.747
ELDERFATHER: We cry
to Thee. O Lord.

277
00:24:07.330 --> 00:24:09.958
Do Thou have mercy upon us?

278
00:24:11.265 --> 00:24:13.243
FAMILY: And grant forgiveness.

279
00:24:13.268 --> 00:24:17.373
ELDERFATHER: O King of heaven.
and everlasting Lord.

280
00:24:17.398 --> 00:24:21.443
receive our prayers
which we pour forth.

281
00:24:22.675 --> 00:24:24.486
FAMILY: And grant forgiveness.

282
00:24:24.597 --> 00:24:29.244
ELDERFATHER: Visit the sick.
bring forth the captive.

283
00:24:29.269 --> 00:24:32.856
help the widow and the orphan.

284
00:24:34.383 --> 00:24:36.904
FAMILY: And grant forgiveness.

285
00:24:36.929 --> 00:24:42.035
ELDERFATHER: We have sinned
and departed from Thee.

286
00:24:42.060 --> 00:24:47.357
Wilt Thou. the Redeemer
of all. save us?

287
00:24:48.197 --> 00:24:50.175
FAMILY: And grant forgiveness.

288
00:24:50.200 --> 00:24:53.096
Have mercy on the penitent

289
00:24:53.121 --> 00:24:57.292
and wash away the stains of sin.

290
00:24:58.825 --> 00:25:00.952
FAMILY: And grant forgiveness.

291
00:25:02.626 --> 00:25:04.378
ALL: Amen.

292
00:25:09.750 --> 00:25:11.812
(EERIE MUSIC PLAYING)

293
00:25:12.043 --> 00:25:14.211
(MUFFLED FIRE CRACKLING)

294
00:25:19.450 --> 00:25:21.160
(DISTANT THUD)

295
00:25:28.917 --> 00:25:30.919
(DISTANT MAN SHOUTS)

296
00:25:32.206 --> 00:25:33.624
(GRUNTS SOFTLY)

297
00:25:36.646 --> 00:25:38.815
(FLAMES WHOOSHING)

298
00:25:49.648 --> 00:25:51.150
MAN 1: Kill him!

299
00:25:52.029 --> 00:25:53.990
(MAN 2 YELLS)

300
00:25:58.424 --> 00:25:59.758
MAN: Godwyn!

301
00:26:01.733 --> 00:26:03.902
-(GRUNTING)
-(ROBIN YELLS)

302
00:26:05.225 --> 00:26:07.770
(ROBIN COUGHING)

303
00:26:09.429 --> 00:26:10.429
(SCREAMS)

304
00:26:12.939 --> 00:26:14.566
(SCREAMING)

305
00:26:16.178 --> 00:26:17.346
(PANTING)

306
00:26:18.621 --> 00:26:20.974
(SCREAMS)

307
00:26:20.999 --> 00:26:23.419
(ROBIN GRUNTS. COUGHS)

308
00:26:23.902 --> 00:26:26.487
-(ROBIN GRUNTS)
-(MAN SCREAMING)

309
00:26:28.596 --> 00:26:30.514
(MAN WHIMPERING LOUDLY)

310
00:26:35.361 --> 00:26:36.839
MAN: No!

311
00:26:36.864 --> 00:26:38.032
(MAN SCREAMS)

312
00:26:39.556 --> 00:26:41.475
(GROANS)

313
00:26:43.111 --> 00:26:44.613
(ROBIN COUGHS)

314
00:26:45.980 --> 00:26:47.482
(MAN GRUNTING)

315
00:26:48.202 --> 00:26:49.453
(BOTH YELLING)

316
00:26:51.062 --> 00:26:52.647
(MAN SCREAMING)

317
00:26:59.675 --> 00:27:01.111
(ROBIN PANTING)

318
00:27:01.136 --> 00:27:03.347
(MAN GROANING)

319
00:27:08.649 --> 00:27:10.692
-(CONTINUES PANTING)
-(MAN GRUNTING IN PANIC)

320
00:27:17.912 --> 00:27:19.413
(BOTH SCREAM)

321
00:27:23.129 --> 00:27:24.964
(ROBIN GASPS. GROANS)

322
00:27:26.151 --> 00:27:27.403
(ROBIN GRUNTS)

323
00:27:28.471 --> 00:27:30.974
(MAN SCREAMING)

324
00:27:33.633 --> 00:27:35.218
(YELLS)

325
00:27:36.596 --> 00:27:38.598
(MAN WHEEZING LOUDLY)

326
00:27:56.079 --> 00:27:57.456
(ROBIN COUGHS)

327
00:28:00.182 --> 00:28:02.351
(MAN GRUNTING WEAKLY)

328
00:28:03.835 --> 00:28:06.605
No. Please. Please.

329
00:28:06.630 --> 00:28:09.692
(CRYING) Please. please!
(SCREAMING)

330
00:28:10.322 --> 00:28:13.325
-(ROBIN YELLS. GRUNTS)
-(FLESH SQUELCHES)

331
00:28:14.884 --> 00:28:16.094
(ROBIN COUGHING)

332
00:28:22.418 --> 00:28:24.503
-(EDWARD SCREAMS)
-(POUNDING ON DOOR)

333
00:28:30.784 --> 00:28:31.784
(EDWARD SCREAMS)

334
00:28:34.250 --> 00:28:37.253
(EDWARD AND
LITTLE MARGARET COUGHING)

335
00:28:39.758 --> 00:28:42.653
-EDWARD: Margaret? Margaret!
-ROBIN: No. no.

336
00:28:42.678 --> 00:28:44.614
No! (BREATHING HEAVILY)

337
00:28:45.017 --> 00:28:46.352
(LITTLE MARGARET COUGHS)

338
00:28:47.150 --> 00:28:49.485
ROBIN: John! Don't!

339
00:28:54.749 --> 00:28:57.085
ELDERFATHER: Little John!

340
00:29:04.241 --> 00:29:08.721
Twenty winters ago.
you murdered my cousin.

341
00:29:08.746 --> 00:29:10.665
Walter of Hathersage.

342
00:29:11.955 --> 00:29:14.808
You have murdered my sons

343
00:29:14.833 --> 00:29:16.460
and my grandson.

344
00:29:17.468 --> 00:29:18.719
As wergild...

345
00:29:19.031 --> 00:29:22.010
I accept your life...

346
00:29:22.261 --> 00:29:25.240
and the life of your daughter.

347
00:29:25.265 --> 00:29:26.558
(ROBIN GRUNTS ANGRILY)

348
00:29:31.048 --> 00:29:33.383
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

349
00:29:33.644 --> 00:29:34.645
(GRUNTS ANGRILY)

350
00:29:39.700 --> 00:29:40.700
(ROBIN GRUNTING)

351
00:29:41.458 --> 00:29:42.458
(ROBIN GROANS)

352
00:30:03.703 --> 00:30:04.746
(MACE SWOOSHING)

353
00:30:06.910 --> 00:30:08.496
(BOTH GRUNTING)

354
00:30:09.993 --> 00:30:11.203
(ROBIN GROANS)

355
00:30:14.272 --> 00:30:15.440
(ROBIN GRUNTING)

356
00:30:18.997 --> 00:30:20.331
(ELDERFATHER GRUNTS)

357
00:30:23.448 --> 00:30:25.533
-(ROBIN GRUNTING)
-(ELDERFATHER GROANING)

358
00:30:27.185 --> 00:30:28.394
(ROBIN GROANS)

359
00:30:33.583 --> 00:30:34.583
(ROBIN GRUNTS)

360
00:30:38.350 --> 00:30:40.516
-(HELMET CLANGS)
-(ROBIN GRUNTS)

361
00:30:40.695 --> 00:30:42.071
(GROANS)

362
00:30:43.432 --> 00:30:46.309
-(ELDERFATHER YELLS)
-(ROBIN SCREAMING)

363
00:30:49.959 --> 00:30:52.003
(GASPING)

364
00:31:03.085 --> 00:31:05.420
-(ELDERFATHER GRUNTS)
-(SCREAMS)

365
00:31:09.756 --> 00:31:12.593
(ROBIN GROANS.
GURGLES AND COUGHS)

366
00:31:16.726 --> 00:31:17.726
(GAGS)

367
00:31:25.634 --> 00:31:27.719
(VOICES WHISPERING INDISTINCTLY)

368
00:31:33.551 --> 00:31:35.222
MAN: (WHISPERING)
heinous crimes...

369
00:31:35.247 --> 00:31:41.839
slayer of man.
woman and child...

370
00:31:42.230 --> 00:31:43.231
(BLOW LANDS)

371
00:31:47.464 --> 00:31:49.091
No...

372
00:31:54.337 --> 00:31:56.022
No...

373
00:31:57.070 --> 00:32:00.561
(ECHOING) No! No! No! No! No!

374
00:32:00.586 --> 00:32:02.421
(YELLING) No!

375
00:32:03.422 --> 00:32:05.215
No!

376
00:32:07.467 --> 00:32:09.845
(CART RATTLING)

377
00:32:12.139 --> 00:32:14.349
(ROBIN BREATHING WEAKLY)

378
00:32:40.793 --> 00:32:43.003
(WIND BLOWING)

379
00:32:53.598 --> 00:32:55.558
(KNIFE SIZZLING)

380
00:32:58.582 --> 00:32:59.934
(FLESH SIZZLING)

381
00:32:59.959 --> 00:33:01.503
(ROBIN SCREAMING)

382
00:33:09.957 --> 00:33:10.850
(ROBIN GROANS)

383
00:33:10.875 --> 00:33:12.961
(INDISTINCT VOICES
CONTINUE WHISPERING)

384
00:33:15.469 --> 00:33:16.762
EDWARD: Robin?

385
00:33:17.841 --> 00:33:21.177
I've heard stories
of a Priory hidden away.

386
00:33:22.877 --> 00:33:24.270
There's a Prioress there

387
00:33:24.294 --> 00:33:26.421
who's older
than anyone remembers...

388
00:33:27.800 --> 00:33:29.343
she has healing magic.

389
00:33:30.712 --> 00:33:32.440
I'll take you to her.

390
00:33:32.465 --> 00:33:34.299
She'll get you well again.

391
00:33:35.350 --> 00:33:37.437
I've heard incredible stories.

392
00:33:39.110 --> 00:33:41.279
(MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING)

393
00:33:49.728 --> 00:33:51.688
(WAVES SPLASHING)

394
00:34:22.449 --> 00:34:24.451
(WIND BLOWING)

395
00:34:32.659 --> 00:34:34.160
(BANGING)

396
00:34:34.842 --> 00:34:37.011
(BREATHING SHALLOW)

397
00:34:38.237 --> 00:34:41.156
Robin. we must leave you.

398
00:34:42.599 --> 00:34:44.149
They'll be hunting us.

399
00:34:45.465 --> 00:34:47.425
(INDISTINCT WHISPERING)

400
00:34:49.454 --> 00:34:51.664
(CONTINUES BREATHING SHALLOW)

401
00:34:57.733 --> 00:34:59.275
(SILENCE)

402
00:35:20.867 --> 00:35:22.328
WOMAN: (ECHOING)
Look at the snow...

403
00:35:25.358 --> 00:35:27.192
it's strange
for it to fall this late.

404
00:35:31.396 --> 00:35:33.230
But it won't stay
on the ground...

405
00:35:36.258 --> 00:35:38.093
and the long days
will soon some.

406
00:35:44.014 --> 00:35:46.559
(GASPS. GROANS)

407
00:35:48.753 --> 00:35:50.838
(SEAGULLS CALLING)

408
00:35:54.052 --> 00:35:56.221
(EXHALES)

409
00:35:57.908 --> 00:35:59.326
(GRUNTS)

410
00:36:02.751 --> 00:36:04.753
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

411
00:36:17.359 --> 00:36:18.776
(DOOR CLOSES)

412
00:36:30.888 --> 00:36:32.306
WOMAN: A man brought you here.

413
00:36:33.809 --> 00:36:35.245
He sealed your wounds with fire

414
00:36:35.270 --> 00:36:37.314
-and he did not do a poor job.
-(GROANS SOFTLY)

415
00:36:38.903 --> 00:36:40.489
You have been here six days.

416
00:36:42.077 --> 00:36:43.787
You have wounds in your abdomen.

417
00:36:44.611 --> 00:36:46.989
Ribs and a leg badly broken.

418
00:36:49.442 --> 00:36:51.444
Do you understand my words?

419
00:36:55.211 --> 00:36:57.147
Where is this?

420
00:36:57.391 --> 00:36:59.619
WOMAN: You're at
the Priory of St. Clement.

421
00:36:59.644 --> 00:37:01.063
We're a place for you to heal.

422
00:37:02.088 --> 00:37:03.714
Wha... What town?

423
00:37:04.515 --> 00:37:05.850
There is no town.

424
00:37:07.667 --> 00:37:09.419
Do you know the story of Saul?

425
00:37:11.520 --> 00:37:12.831
What?

426
00:37:13.061 --> 00:37:16.207
It goes. there once
was a man. Saul...

427
00:37:16.232 --> 00:37:19.569
a breather of menaces
against disciples of the Lord.

428
00:37:20.329 --> 00:37:22.140
He came to the Prince of Priests

429
00:37:22.165 --> 00:37:24.560
and asked of him
letters into Damascus.

430
00:37:24.585 --> 00:37:25.979
to the synagogues.

431
00:37:26.004 --> 00:37:27.357
That if he came across

432
00:37:27.382 --> 00:37:29.277
any man or woman of this life.
he should lead them bound

433
00:37:29.301 --> 00:37:30.677
-and...
-(ROBIN GRUNTS)

434
00:37:32.451 --> 00:37:34.453
That is all we need to do.

435
00:37:35.146 --> 00:37:36.689
-Just a few drops.
-(BLOOD DRIPPING)

436
00:37:39.273 --> 00:37:41.067
It was not too painful?

437
00:37:43.017 --> 00:37:44.268
It were not.

438
00:37:48.780 --> 00:37:50.073
I'm Sister Brigid.

439
00:37:51.257 --> 00:37:52.676
What's your name?

440
00:37:54.785 --> 00:37:55.995
Randolph.

441
00:38:00.358 --> 00:38:03.027
Well. I owe you
an apology. Randolph.

442
00:38:03.688 --> 00:38:05.190
What apology?

443
00:38:07.322 --> 00:38:09.241
You begged for me
to let you die.

444
00:38:11.231 --> 00:38:12.523
And I did not.

445
00:38:14.793 --> 00:38:15.855
You said it was right.

446
00:38:15.880 --> 00:38:17.131
I were with fever.

447
00:38:19.320 --> 00:38:21.114
Well. your fever has passed.

448
00:38:22.524 --> 00:38:23.935
Rest now. Randolph.

449
00:38:47.290 --> 00:38:50.418
MAN: Your body
is covered in scars.

450
00:38:50.979 --> 00:38:53.147
(ROBIN GASPING SOFTLY)

451
00:39:07.424 --> 00:39:09.760
Do you mean anyone
at this Priory harm?

452
00:39:13.753 --> 00:39:14.963
I do not.

453
00:39:25.154 --> 00:39:28.199
THE LEPER: Will any harm
follow you here?

454
00:39:29.928 --> 00:39:31.221
It will not.

455
00:39:40.416 --> 00:39:43.336
THE LEPER: (SOFTLY)
You will do them no harm.

456
00:39:57.156 --> 00:39:58.156
(DOOR CLOSES)

457
00:40:02.615 --> 00:40:04.158
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

458
00:40:15.646 --> 00:40:17.792
SISTER BRIGID:
Now back to the bed.

459
00:40:17.817 --> 00:40:20.444
(SLOW. LIMPING FOOTSTEPS)

460
00:40:24.885 --> 00:40:27.137
(ROBIN GRUNTING)

461
00:40:30.275 --> 00:40:31.944
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

462
00:40:32.717 --> 00:40:34.135
Now back to the door.

463
00:40:39.597 --> 00:40:41.766
(ROBIN GRUNTING)

464
00:41:02.315 --> 00:41:03.981
SISTER BRIGID:
Now open the door.

465
00:41:04.006 --> 00:41:05.590
(ROBIN BREATHING HEAVILY)

466
00:41:11.859 --> 00:41:13.819
(INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING)

467
00:41:22.689 --> 00:41:24.273
Go as far as you'd like.

468
00:41:26.949 --> 00:41:29.159
(CONTINUES BREATHING HEAVILY)

469
00:41:38.872 --> 00:41:41.082
(BREATHING HEAVILY. GRUNTING)

470
00:42:03.278 --> 00:42:05.154
(BIRD CHIRPING)

471
00:42:06.807 --> 00:42:08.976
(SERENE MUSIC PLAYING)

472
00:42:18.437 --> 00:42:20.606
(DISTANT ANIMAL CALLING)

473
00:42:30.284 --> 00:42:32.286
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

474
00:42:50.387 --> 00:42:52.599
(CHILDREN LAUGHING. CHATTERING)

475
00:42:57.436 --> 00:42:59.646
(GOATS BLEATING)

476
00:43:05.366 --> 00:43:07.535
(CHATTERING CONTINUES)

477
00:43:12.177 --> 00:43:14.072
WOMAN: William. careful. please.

478
00:43:14.097 --> 00:43:16.391
(BOY SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

479
00:43:18.522 --> 00:43:20.524
(GROANS. BREATHES HEAVILY)

480
00:43:22.365 --> 00:43:23.605
SISTER BRIGID: Can you row yet?

481
00:43:26.331 --> 00:43:28.434
There is a boat
on the west shore.

482
00:43:28.459 --> 00:43:30.895
(PANTING)

483
00:43:30.920 --> 00:43:32.171
That's all right.

484
00:43:33.505 --> 00:43:35.983
You can stay here
if you help in the orchard.

485
00:43:36.008 --> 00:43:38.010
Oh. I'm... not a farmer.

486
00:43:38.871 --> 00:43:40.498
Then you know not how to hunt.

487
00:43:40.949 --> 00:43:42.409
Aye. I know how to hunt.

488
00:43:43.683 --> 00:43:46.537
There is some game
on this island.

489
00:43:46.562 --> 00:43:50.167
But no. you cannot hunt.
You cannot even draw a bow.

490
00:43:50.192 --> 00:43:52.844
-I can draw my bow.
-It's mostly rabbits.

491
00:43:52.869 --> 00:43:55.622
-Do you know how to trap?
-I know how to trap.

492
00:43:56.923 --> 00:43:59.068
Good. But no more than six traps

493
00:43:59.093 --> 00:44:01.095
or the population
will not sustain.

494
00:44:01.743 --> 00:44:03.287
Can you manage six traps?

495
00:44:07.954 --> 00:44:09.414
I can manage six traps.

496
00:44:11.386 --> 00:44:12.429
Good.

497
00:44:13.961 --> 00:44:16.839
Then the rest of your time.
you may help in the orchard.

498
00:44:20.919 --> 00:44:23.296
-(WAVES SPLASHING)
-(SEAGULLS CALLING)

499
00:44:33.080 --> 00:44:34.081
(GRUNTS)

500
00:44:35.007 --> 00:44:36.049
(GROANS)

501
00:44:40.311 --> 00:44:41.728
(GRUNTS)

502
00:44:42.609 --> 00:44:44.527
(GROANS)

503
00:44:45.786 --> 00:44:47.538
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

504
00:44:52.961 --> 00:44:54.754
THE LEPER: Are you
trying to flee?

505
00:44:58.793 --> 00:45:00.087
You are quiet.

506
00:45:01.772 --> 00:45:03.941
THE LEPER: I am quiet and slow.

507
00:45:05.389 --> 00:45:08.951
You are quiet.
but you need to be slow.

508
00:45:08.975 --> 00:45:10.120
You're a cripple.

509
00:45:10.144 --> 00:45:11.853
Aye. you're a leper.

510
00:45:12.771 --> 00:45:16.501
THE LEPER: It is all right
to be slow. We are safe here.

511
00:45:16.525 --> 00:45:19.171
ROBIN: That's quite a thing
to say. You know that?

512
00:45:19.195 --> 00:45:21.256
THE LEPER: I know that
because she has made us safe.

513
00:45:21.280 --> 00:45:22.656
ROBIN: Oh. your Prioress?

514
00:45:25.035 --> 00:45:26.328
THE LEPER: She were like us.

515
00:45:27.369 --> 00:45:31.457
She knew great sorrow.
Great pain.

516
00:45:32.121 --> 00:45:33.372
Widowed young.

517
00:45:35.488 --> 00:45:37.008
But through that sorrow.

518
00:45:37.033 --> 00:45:39.219
she found the strength
to heal us.

519
00:45:39.244 --> 00:45:41.847
Well. you do not look
like you've been healed.

520
00:45:42.050 --> 00:45:43.510
(THE LEPER CHUCKLES)

521
00:45:45.324 --> 00:45:47.501
The Prioress once told me
a story

522
00:45:47.526 --> 00:45:49.528
of a great philosopher...

523
00:45:50.340 --> 00:45:53.010
the greatest philosopher
of his time.

524
00:45:54.001 --> 00:45:57.398
But one day.
his king turned against him.

525
00:45:57.423 --> 00:46:00.509
Threw him in a dungeon
to be tortured and executed.

526
00:46:01.867 --> 00:46:03.930
But in his misery.

527
00:46:03.955 --> 00:46:07.059
when he had nothing.
an angel came

528
00:46:07.084 --> 00:46:09.336
to the philosopher
and she spoke to him.

529
00:46:10.454 --> 00:46:12.307
And from her.

530
00:46:12.332 --> 00:46:14.936
he learned
that it did not matter

531
00:46:14.961 --> 00:46:17.546
if this whole world
were misery...

532
00:46:19.356 --> 00:46:21.400
if all he had were death.

533
00:46:23.015 --> 00:46:25.035
Because he had one thing

534
00:46:25.060 --> 00:46:27.395
that could never be
touched or taken.

535
00:46:29.914 --> 00:46:31.248
He had his mind.

536
00:46:33.110 --> 00:46:34.361
And in his mind...

537
00:46:36.165 --> 00:46:37.499
he had God.

538
00:46:40.122 --> 00:46:43.666
It's never too late
to find peace. (GRUNTS)

539
00:46:44.489 --> 00:46:45.840
What are you doing?

540
00:46:45.864 --> 00:46:48.801
THE LEPER: (GROANS) Ah.
I row across every day.

541
00:46:48.825 --> 00:46:50.720
Your friend was strong enough
to take you.

542
00:46:50.745 --> 00:46:52.621
but some are not.
so I ferry them.

543
00:46:52.663 --> 00:46:55.390
-Will you take me across?
-I will not.

544
00:46:55.415 --> 00:46:58.519
You can row yourself
when you're stronger.

545
00:46:58.544 --> 00:47:01.398
For now. work at your tasks.
Trapping. I hear.

546
00:47:01.423 --> 00:47:03.675
-I will hunt.
-No. you can't hunt.

547
00:47:05.574 --> 00:47:07.159
(THE LEPER GRUNTS)

548
00:47:09.083 --> 00:47:10.685
ROBIN: Leper.

549
00:47:10.710 --> 00:47:13.130
what happened
to that great philosopher?

550
00:47:13.943 --> 00:47:16.946
He were tortured
and executed. of course.

551
00:47:18.320 --> 00:47:19.362
Of course.

552
00:47:24.435 --> 00:47:25.870
(LAUGHTER AND CHATTER)

553
00:47:25.895 --> 00:47:28.457
THE LEPER: ♪ Sumer is icumen
In loude sing cuccu! ♪

554
00:47:28.482 --> 00:47:30.835
♪ Groweth seed
and bloweth meed ♪

555
00:47:30.860 --> 00:47:33.359
♪ And springth the wode now ♪

556
00:47:33.384 --> 00:47:35.529
♪ Sing cuccu ♪

557
00:47:35.554 --> 00:47:38.697
♪ Ewe bleteth after lamb
Loweth after calve cow ♪

558
00:47:38.722 --> 00:47:40.890
(MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING)

559
00:48:18.103 --> 00:48:20.230
(MUSIC CONTINUES)

560
00:48:36.947 --> 00:48:39.157
(BREATHING SHARPLY)

561
00:48:42.898 --> 00:48:45.441
-(GRUNTING)
-(BOWSTRING STRETCHES)

562
00:48:47.651 --> 00:48:49.612
-(BOWSTRING TWANGS)
-(BREATHING HEAVILY)

563
00:48:53.008 --> 00:48:55.027
(GRUNTING)

564
00:48:55.052 --> 00:48:57.179
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

565
00:48:59.517 --> 00:49:00.518
(GROANS)

566
00:49:01.674 --> 00:49:03.342
(GRUNTING)

567
00:49:04.375 --> 00:49:06.062
-(GROANS)
-(ARROW THUDS)

568
00:49:06.087 --> 00:49:07.230
-(YELLS)
-(BOW CLATTERS)

569
00:49:07.255 --> 00:49:09.424
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

570
00:49:11.663 --> 00:49:13.540
(BOY YELLING INDISTINCTLY)

571
00:49:20.023 --> 00:49:22.293
ROBIN: Oi! Oi!

572
00:49:22.318 --> 00:49:24.361
The Leper has brought someone!

573
00:49:24.865 --> 00:49:26.617
From the far shore!

574
00:49:58.870 --> 00:50:00.330
(LITTLE MARGARET
BREATHES HEAVILY)

575
00:50:06.509 --> 00:50:07.845
LITTLE MARGARET: Papa's dead.

576
00:50:11.066 --> 00:50:12.734
(SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING)

577
00:50:32.297 --> 00:50:34.608
(GRASS RUSTLING)

578
00:50:34.645 --> 00:50:36.605
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

579
00:50:38.676 --> 00:50:40.845
(RABBIT'S LEGS THUMPING)

580
00:50:56.799 --> 00:50:58.551
(LEGS THUMPING FRANTICALLY)

581
00:51:01.776 --> 00:51:03.486
-(BONES CRACK)
-(THUMPING STOPS)

582
00:51:05.307 --> 00:51:06.893
(RECEDING FOOTSTEPS)

583
00:51:12.790 --> 00:51:13.874
(CROW CAWS)

584
00:51:15.674 --> 00:51:16.883
(ROBIN GROANS SOFTLY)

585
00:51:23.187 --> 00:51:24.730
How's the girl?

586
00:51:38.180 --> 00:51:40.182
THE LEPER: Let me show you
my trees.

587
00:51:50.523 --> 00:51:53.710
These are the elderberries.

588
00:51:53.735 --> 00:51:56.506
They harvest late in the summer.

589
00:51:56.531 --> 00:51:58.372
ROBIN: Do they know
what you were before this?

590
00:51:58.397 --> 00:52:00.583
THE LEPER: Oh. you'll have
to favor this side

591
00:52:00.608 --> 00:52:01.776
for my hearing.

592
00:52:04.390 --> 00:52:07.142
Pears. I harvest just after.

593
00:52:10.061 --> 00:52:12.124
And what were I before this?

594
00:52:12.149 --> 00:52:13.876
ROBIN: Oh. a sell sword at best.

595
00:52:13.901 --> 00:52:16.279
THE LEPER: (CHUCKLING)
Aye. at best. certainly.

596
00:52:17.327 --> 00:52:18.703
We have a way about us!

597
00:52:20.004 --> 00:52:21.482
You remember the trees?

598
00:52:21.507 --> 00:52:23.967
-Pears and elderberries.
-THE LEPER: Wonderful.

599
00:52:26.700 --> 00:52:27.993
Some of them know.

600
00:52:29.482 --> 00:52:32.693
But the Prioress does not care
who we were.

601
00:52:34.770 --> 00:52:37.232
And the apples harvest
in the autumn.

602
00:52:38.650 --> 00:52:41.737
ROBIN: Did she. uh.
speak of what happened to her?

603
00:52:43.386 --> 00:52:45.449
THE LEPER: Well. the Prioress
is tending to the girl.

604
00:52:45.473 --> 00:52:48.351
You should speak with her.
if you are concerned.

605
00:52:51.639 --> 00:52:52.890
What were the trees?

606
00:52:54.825 --> 00:52:57.245
ROBIN: Pears. apples
and elderberries.

607
00:52:59.150 --> 00:53:00.360
THE LEPER: Wonderful.

608
00:53:01.515 --> 00:53:02.516
(DOOR CLOSES)

609
00:53:11.996 --> 00:53:13.830
SISTER BRIGID: This will be
your last letting.

610
00:53:15.365 --> 00:53:17.576
Though your body
still has much healing.

611
00:53:21.248 --> 00:53:22.332
You're tired.

612
00:53:23.447 --> 00:53:24.490
I am.

613
00:53:25.997 --> 00:53:27.499
But I have been tired before.

614
00:53:29.482 --> 00:53:31.124
The child does not sleep.

615
00:53:34.478 --> 00:53:35.855
What happened to her?

616
00:53:37.454 --> 00:53:39.130
Terrible things.

617
00:53:41.964 --> 00:53:45.152
-She told you her story?
-No. she does not speak.

618
00:53:45.177 --> 00:53:47.429
She does not eat
and she does not sleep.

619
00:53:51.820 --> 00:53:54.073
-(SKIN PRICKS)
-(BLOOD DRIPPING)

620
00:53:54.906 --> 00:53:56.241
What is her name?

621
00:54:03.961 --> 00:54:05.213
Margaret.

622
00:54:08.195 --> 00:54:09.487
Who is she?

623
00:54:11.639 --> 00:54:14.558
I met her father. A farmer.

624
00:54:15.816 --> 00:54:17.586
SISTER BRIGID: Well. he's dead.

625
00:54:17.611 --> 00:54:18.671
It seems.

626
00:54:18.974 --> 00:54:20.411
And the mother?

627
00:54:20.436 --> 00:54:23.290
-Ah. I think dead.
-How?

628
00:54:23.315 --> 00:54:25.400
I don't know. Dead past.

629
00:54:26.119 --> 00:54:27.120
Slain?

630
00:54:28.411 --> 00:54:29.453
Perhaps.

631
00:54:34.937 --> 00:54:36.313
You lie very well.

632
00:54:39.072 --> 00:54:40.740
(BLOOD STOPS DRIPPING)

633
00:54:45.813 --> 00:54:47.107
Did the child see?

634
00:54:49.606 --> 00:54:51.066
She could have.

635
00:54:53.773 --> 00:54:55.796
That is much for a child to see.

636
00:54:58.519 --> 00:54:59.728
(SIGHS)

637
00:55:05.590 --> 00:55:07.050
I'm sorry for your friend.

638
00:55:11.644 --> 00:55:12.854
Thank you.

639
00:55:14.305 --> 00:55:16.515
Would you like me
to pray for him?

640
00:55:20.549 --> 00:55:21.967
As you wish.

641
00:55:25.465 --> 00:55:26.591
What was his name?

642
00:55:31.210 --> 00:55:32.294
Edward.

643
00:55:34.606 --> 00:55:35.900
SISTER BRIGID: Edward.

644
00:55:39.094 --> 00:55:40.654
Be not your heart afraid.

645
00:55:40.679 --> 00:55:41.907
for ye believe in God

646
00:55:41.956 --> 00:55:43.290
and ye believe in me.

647
00:55:45.189 --> 00:55:48.025
In the house of my father.
there are many rooms.

648
00:55:49.412 --> 00:55:52.474
And when I make ready
for you a place.

649
00:55:52.499 --> 00:55:54.835
I shall come
and take thee to myself.

650
00:55:56.030 --> 00:55:59.033
For where I am. He may be also.

651
00:56:01.357 --> 00:56:03.567
And whither I go.
He shall know the way.

652
00:56:06.999 --> 00:56:08.667
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATIONS)

653
00:56:09.020 --> 00:56:11.398
(BOY SCREAMING. CRYING LOUDLY)

654
00:56:15.119 --> 00:56:17.331
(BOY CONTINUES SCREAMING
AND CRYING)

655
00:56:24.921 --> 00:56:26.394
-THE LEPER: She has a knife.
-SISTER BRIGID: Margaret!

656
00:56:26.418 --> 00:56:27.813
She stabbed me!

657
00:56:28.097 --> 00:56:29.598
SISTER BRIGID: Margaret!

658
00:56:31.847 --> 00:56:33.867
-(BOY CONTINUES CRYING)
-It's all right.

659
00:56:33.892 --> 00:56:35.036
(LITTLE MARGARET
BREATHING HEAVILY)

660
00:56:35.060 --> 00:56:37.247
Margaret. it's...
it's all right.

661
00:56:37.272 --> 00:56:39.272
-Margaret. it's all right.
-(LITTLE MARGARET CRIES)

662
00:56:42.593 --> 00:56:44.279
THE LEPER: She don't know
this island.

663
00:56:44.304 --> 00:56:46.014
There are boar about.

664
00:56:47.115 --> 00:56:48.467
(SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING)

665
00:56:48.492 --> 00:56:50.055
-THE LEPER: Margaret!
-SISTER BRIGID: Margaret!

666
00:56:50.079 --> 00:56:51.890
-(WIND BLOWING)
-SISTER BRIGID: Margaret!

667
00:56:51.915 --> 00:56:54.811
-WOMAN: Margaret!
-SISTER BRIGID: Margaret!

668
00:56:54.836 --> 00:56:56.378
WOMAN: Margaret!

669
00:56:59.013 --> 00:57:00.973
(WIND WHOOSHING)

670
00:57:02.499 --> 00:57:04.292
(FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING)

671
00:57:26.873 --> 00:57:28.500
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

672
00:57:53.857 --> 00:57:56.109
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

673
00:58:27.102 --> 00:58:28.270
(GRUNTS SOFTLY)

674
00:58:41.937 --> 00:58:43.147
Oi.

675
00:58:45.694 --> 00:58:46.737
Oi!

676
00:58:46.762 --> 00:58:48.556
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

677
00:58:55.165 --> 00:58:56.333
Give it.

678
00:59:05.756 --> 00:59:07.216
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

679
00:59:09.990 --> 00:59:11.241
Give it.

680
00:59:28.547 --> 00:59:30.214
Those men that hurt you.

681
00:59:33.503 --> 00:59:35.016
do they know you're here?

682
00:59:40.129 --> 00:59:41.130
Hmm.

683
00:59:48.173 --> 00:59:49.550
What's my name?

684
00:59:55.382 --> 00:59:56.737
Say my name.

685
00:59:58.774 --> 01:00:00.025
Randolph.

686
01:00:03.242 --> 01:00:04.618
(SIGHS)

687
01:00:05.466 --> 01:00:06.717
That's right.

688
01:00:12.049 --> 01:00:13.801
Who's Little John?

689
01:00:16.151 --> 01:00:19.620
That name is nonsense
and you should never speak it.

690
01:00:19.645 --> 01:00:22.248
And if you speak it.
a cat will come in the night

691
01:00:22.273 --> 01:00:23.375
and take your tongue.

692
01:00:23.400 --> 01:00:25.569
(BREATH TREMBLING)

693
01:00:30.408 --> 01:00:31.409
(SIGHS)

694
01:00:33.327 --> 01:00:34.412
It's all right.

695
01:00:37.498 --> 01:00:38.707
Go to sleep.

696
01:00:40.876 --> 01:00:43.046
(WIND WHISTLING)

697
01:00:46.235 --> 01:00:47.966
ROBIN: I'll watch the storm.

698
01:00:51.804 --> 01:00:53.889
All right. lay down.

699
01:00:57.726 --> 01:00:58.978
Close your eyes.

700
01:01:04.192 --> 01:01:05.234
You can sleep.

701
01:01:10.489 --> 01:01:11.782
Sleep.

702
01:01:50.279 --> 01:01:52.448
SISTER BRIGID: Thank you
for bringing her back.

703
01:01:54.825 --> 01:01:56.077
It were nothing.

704
01:02:01.415 --> 01:02:03.928
Do you know the story
of this Priory?

705
01:02:04.585 --> 01:02:05.836
ROBIN: No.

706
01:02:08.172 --> 01:02:10.067
Well. in ages before history.

707
01:02:10.091 --> 01:02:11.693
this was a holy site

708
01:02:11.717 --> 01:02:13.665
of the ancient Druids.

709
01:02:15.263 --> 01:02:17.181
They worshipped unknown gods.

710
01:02:18.891 --> 01:02:20.743
Worshipped in these woods.

711
01:02:21.978 --> 01:02:24.456
Then the Romans came long ago.
and they sensed

712
01:02:24.480 --> 01:02:25.790
the magic of this place.

713
01:02:25.814 --> 01:02:27.868
so they built their temples.

714
01:02:29.360 --> 01:02:31.130
And people upon people
sensed it.

715
01:02:31.154 --> 01:02:33.156
and they came here to worship.

716
01:02:34.646 --> 01:02:36.374
Countless gods.
tribe after tribe.

717
01:02:36.399 --> 01:02:39.235
who would not even know
how to speak to each other.

718
01:02:40.496 --> 01:02:42.819
Yet we were all
pulled to this place.

719
01:02:44.792 --> 01:02:47.420
ROBIN: Do you believe
there is magic in this island?

720
01:02:49.923 --> 01:02:51.590
I believe there is power in it.

721
01:02:54.427 --> 01:02:56.637
I have seen
the power in stories.

722
01:02:59.307 --> 01:03:02.601
They can be used to make men
do terrible things.

723
01:03:03.686 --> 01:03:07.648
And then those terrible things
become stories.

724
01:03:08.903 --> 01:03:10.113
And stories...

725
01:03:14.363 --> 01:03:15.364
No.

726
01:03:16.240 --> 01:03:17.741
You cannot trust any of them.

727
01:03:18.655 --> 01:03:20.491
We cannot be trusted with them.

728
01:03:22.783 --> 01:03:25.576
Knives cut bread
as well as they do flesh.

729
01:03:27.460 --> 01:03:29.128
It's a question of balance.

730
01:03:30.004 --> 01:03:31.714
ROBIN: Does balance have a say?

731
01:03:34.258 --> 01:03:36.677
I think if balance
did not have some say.

732
01:03:37.646 --> 01:03:39.107
we would not be here.

733
01:03:41.461 --> 01:03:45.298
This world would not...
be here and...

734
01:03:46.645 --> 01:03:48.772
we would not be
sharing these words.

735
01:03:49.834 --> 01:03:51.252
And do you ever consider that?

736
01:03:53.378 --> 01:03:55.064
The incredible precision
of balance

737
01:03:55.089 --> 01:03:57.591
over such an expanse of time.

738
01:03:59.245 --> 01:04:03.475
The balance it takes to create
a word. any specific word.

739
01:04:03.500 --> 01:04:06.336
That can pass
between lips and...

740
01:04:08.077 --> 01:04:10.370
be understood by two minds.

741
01:04:17.781 --> 01:04:19.074
Randolph.

742
01:04:22.975 --> 01:04:24.268
Thank you.

743
01:05:05.585 --> 01:05:06.752
(ROBIN GRUNTS)

744
01:05:30.021 --> 01:05:31.814
-ROBIN: Mmm. Mmm.
-SISTER BRIGID: Mmm.

745
01:05:43.194 --> 01:05:44.236
Not hungry?

746
01:05:46.297 --> 01:05:47.464
No?

747
01:06:20.166 --> 01:06:21.668
THE LEPER: I'll be dying soon.

748
01:06:23.357 --> 01:06:24.400
ROBIN: How do you know?

749
01:06:26.957 --> 01:06:28.918
THE LEPER: I can feel it inside.

750
01:06:31.408 --> 01:06:33.243
ROBIN: What does it feel like?

751
01:06:35.364 --> 01:06:37.033
THE LEPER: It feels right.

752
01:06:40.632 --> 01:06:42.801
(SEAGULL SQUAWKING)

753
01:06:48.574 --> 01:06:50.117
There's someone there.

754
01:06:52.921 --> 01:06:54.915
THE LEPER: The waters
have been busy.

755
01:06:58.328 --> 01:06:59.622
ROBIN: Start around the feet.

756
01:06:59.902 --> 01:07:01.111
Little cuts.

757
01:07:01.449 --> 01:07:03.134
Good. Other one.

758
01:07:04.666 --> 01:07:06.918
All right. Oh.

759
01:07:08.979 --> 01:07:10.188
(SOFTLY) Okay.

760
01:07:10.751 --> 01:07:12.312
Good.

761
01:07:12.337 --> 01:07:14.064
Right. now.
let's do down the front.

762
01:07:14.127 --> 01:07:15.921
Right down on the belly. Good.

763
01:07:16.689 --> 01:07:18.709
Right. Give me.

764
01:07:18.960 --> 01:07:20.896
Right. Watch this one.

765
01:07:20.921 --> 01:07:23.650
Just like... just like that.

766
01:07:23.675 --> 01:07:25.344
That's it. You do the other one.

767
01:07:26.734 --> 01:07:29.087
That's it. that's it. that's it.

768
01:07:29.112 --> 01:07:30.113
Pull.

769
01:07:33.115 --> 01:07:35.285
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

770
01:07:41.021 --> 01:07:43.191
(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)

771
01:07:48.226 --> 01:07:50.019
(SISTER BRIGID
SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

772
01:08:05.808 --> 01:08:08.102
SISTER BRIGID: You are a brave
young man.

773
01:08:08.815 --> 01:08:10.458
ARTHUR: Thank you. sister.

774
01:08:11.980 --> 01:08:13.357
Are you hungry. Arthur?

775
01:08:14.356 --> 01:08:17.376
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

776
01:08:17.401 --> 01:08:18.920
I am. sister.

777
01:08:18.945 --> 01:08:21.591
Well. Sarah will fix you up
a good supper tonight.

778
01:08:21.616 --> 01:08:23.993
Herring stew. Herring stew.

779
01:08:25.847 --> 01:08:28.785
-Do you like that?
-Yes.

780
01:08:28.810 --> 01:08:30.228
Where do you come from. Arthur?

781
01:08:34.205 --> 01:08:35.891
My family farm toward Keswick.

782
01:08:35.916 --> 01:08:38.061
-ROBIN: Toward Keswick?
-Yes. Sir.

783
01:08:38.086 --> 01:08:40.981
-Randolph.
-Randolph. Toward Keswick.

784
01:08:41.006 --> 01:08:43.008
The Leper said
you seek your niece.

785
01:08:43.834 --> 01:08:45.680
-I do.
-You were set upon?

786
01:08:47.875 --> 01:08:49.419
-I was.
-On the road?

787
01:08:50.943 --> 01:08:52.170
Yes.

788
01:08:52.195 --> 01:08:53.947
-You are safe here.
-Which road?

789
01:08:56.023 --> 01:08:57.484
The road to Keswick. Sir.

790
01:08:59.221 --> 01:09:00.949
Thank the Lord you survived.

791
01:09:00.974 --> 01:09:02.327
I do thank the Lord.

792
01:09:02.352 --> 01:09:04.162
How about honeyed pears
after supper

793
01:09:04.187 --> 01:09:05.648
for being so brave?

794
01:09:08.501 --> 01:09:10.753
-Thank you. sister.
-Good.

795
01:09:24.259 --> 01:09:25.510
Little Margaret.

796
01:09:27.119 --> 01:09:28.638
That man. Arthur.

797
01:09:28.663 --> 01:09:31.500
Did you ever see him
before you came to the Priory?

798
01:09:34.953 --> 01:09:35.954
Margaret.

799
01:09:43.129 --> 01:09:47.047
The men...
The men who hurt your papa.

800
01:09:49.436 --> 01:09:51.063
Did you see their faces?

801
01:09:52.329 --> 01:09:53.872
Papa said to run.

802
01:09:55.207 --> 01:09:56.541
(LITTLE MARGARET SIGHS)

803
01:10:04.710 --> 01:10:06.332
Papa stopped praying.

804
01:10:07.992 --> 01:10:09.095
He was angry.

805
01:10:09.120 --> 01:10:10.722
(SIGHS. MUTTERS)

806
01:10:10.747 --> 01:10:12.166
He prayed in his mind.

807
01:10:15.209 --> 01:10:16.499
What's Papa's name?

808
01:10:18.594 --> 01:10:19.762
(ARROW THUDS)

809
01:10:20.869 --> 01:10:22.205
Your papa's your papa.

810
01:10:34.932 --> 01:10:36.142
Bring it here.

811
01:10:38.068 --> 01:10:39.235
(ROBIN GRUNTS SOFTLY)

812
01:10:45.588 --> 01:10:47.903
Oh. this is fine work.

813
01:10:51.924 --> 01:10:53.301
Oh.

814
01:10:53.503 --> 01:10:55.616
You see it favors a bend here.

815
01:10:57.059 --> 01:11:00.812
Oh. aye. Now you have to
balance it so it bends evenly.

816
01:11:02.032 --> 01:11:05.828
So this part here needs
to be thinned. All right?

817
01:11:11.065 --> 01:11:12.524
Can you make for me?

818
01:11:15.301 --> 01:11:16.719
You want me to make you a bow?

819
01:11:21.221 --> 01:11:22.263
All right.

820
01:11:23.905 --> 01:11:25.116
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

821
01:11:30.472 --> 01:11:31.993
SISTER BRIGID: Today.
I remembered a story

822
01:11:32.017 --> 01:11:34.370
by a poet named Lucretius.

823
01:11:34.434 --> 01:11:35.518
(FIRE CRACKLES)

824
01:11:36.228 --> 01:11:38.469
He wrote on
what are called atoms.

825
01:11:40.070 --> 01:11:42.006
Where if you pick apart
the trees

826
01:11:42.031 --> 01:11:43.842
and people and stones.

827
01:11:43.867 --> 01:11:47.305
these would be the smallest
invisible pieces

828
01:11:47.330 --> 01:11:50.917
that make up
everything in creation.

829
01:11:53.017 --> 01:11:57.479
And these atoms are sailing
through the void and...

830
01:12:00.144 --> 01:12:01.955
well. sometimes.
for no reason at all.

831
01:12:01.980 --> 01:12:03.314
they change their course.

832
01:12:06.263 --> 01:12:08.474
The least amount.
not even a hair.

833
01:12:13.393 --> 01:12:17.272
And if it weren't
for that small...

834
01:12:17.999 --> 01:12:21.979
unpredictable change
forcing the atoms to cross

835
01:12:22.004 --> 01:12:23.964
and weave with each other...

836
01:12:27.100 --> 01:12:29.936
nothing at all
under the heavens would exist.

837
01:12:31.948 --> 01:12:33.449
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

838
01:13:22.479 --> 01:13:23.856
(INCENSE SIZZLES)

839
01:13:27.039 --> 01:13:29.917
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

840
01:13:39.224 --> 01:13:40.935
(EXHALES)

841
01:13:41.465 --> 01:13:44.010
(BREATHING DEEPLY)

842
01:13:50.471 --> 01:13:52.681
(MOANING SOFTLY)

843
01:14:25.406 --> 01:14:28.034
(GASPING SOFTLY)

844
01:14:33.059 --> 01:14:35.103
(EXHALES SHARPLY)

845
01:14:35.934 --> 01:14:37.102
(MOANS AND GASPS)

846
01:14:53.065 --> 01:14:54.817
(EXHALES DEEPLY)

847
01:15:13.905 --> 01:15:15.924
ROBIN: Yes. Good.

848
01:15:16.302 --> 01:15:17.720
-(CHUCKLES)
-Harder.

849
01:15:17.745 --> 01:15:19.393
That's it. Good.

850
01:15:19.418 --> 01:15:22.514
-(LAUGHS)
-(CHUCKLES)

851
01:15:22.539 --> 01:15:24.749
That's good. Harder.

852
01:15:25.410 --> 01:15:26.845
Let me help you.

853
01:15:26.870 --> 01:15:28.348
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

854
01:15:28.373 --> 01:15:30.056
ROBIN: Grab that one.

855
01:15:30.912 --> 01:15:33.197
Good. There we go!

856
01:15:33.221 --> 01:15:34.518
(CHUCKLES) Good.

857
01:15:34.543 --> 01:15:36.545
(CHILDREN CHATTERING)

858
01:15:37.725 --> 01:15:39.493
Which one do you think
for your bow?

859
01:15:40.145 --> 01:15:41.586
(MUMBLES) Let's hold and look.

860
01:15:42.447 --> 01:15:43.448
Okay.

861
01:15:44.254 --> 01:15:46.357
There we go. They're both good.

862
01:15:46.382 --> 01:15:47.742
(LITTLE MARGARET
SIGHS CONTENTEDLY)

863
01:15:48.883 --> 01:15:50.302
(CHATTER CONTINUES)

864
01:15:57.578 --> 01:15:59.306
BOY: Margaret!

865
01:15:59.330 --> 01:16:00.932
Margaret! Come and play!

866
01:16:00.956 --> 01:16:03.168
(CHILDREN CHATTERING
INDISTINCTLY)

867
01:16:07.338 --> 01:16:10.090
(CHILDREN LAUGHING
AND CHATTERING)

868
01:16:22.478 --> 01:16:24.439
(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)

869
01:16:28.943 --> 01:16:30.528
(CHATTER CONTINUES)

870
01:16:41.414 --> 01:16:42.415
ROBIN: Arthur.

871
01:16:43.791 --> 01:16:45.352
Do you know how to trap?

872
01:16:45.376 --> 01:16:47.062
-Yes.
-Good.

873
01:16:47.086 --> 01:16:49.130
I need a strong hand. Come.

874
01:17:02.268 --> 01:17:03.936
ROBIN:
Does your family have land?

875
01:17:05.646 --> 01:17:06.646
Yes.

876
01:17:08.691 --> 01:17:10.307
ROBIN: How many
of you are there?

877
01:17:12.112 --> 01:17:13.539
ARTHUR: I don't know.

878
01:17:16.509 --> 01:17:18.094
(GRUNTS. GROANS)

879
01:17:20.286 --> 01:17:21.686
-ARTHUR: Are you all right?
-(SIGHS)

880
01:17:23.244 --> 01:17:24.846
I am. I am.

881
01:17:24.871 --> 01:17:27.117
Just not as young
as I once were.

882
01:17:28.378 --> 01:17:29.605
(SIGHS)

883
01:17:29.629 --> 01:17:31.214
I could use a hand up is all.

884
01:17:33.383 --> 01:17:35.050
(GRUNTS. GROANS)

885
01:17:36.051 --> 01:17:37.262
Thank you.

886
01:17:38.888 --> 01:17:40.931
Oh aye. they delivered you
quite a blow.

887
01:17:42.933 --> 01:17:44.508
-Yes.
-Who did it?

888
01:17:46.854 --> 01:17:48.106
A man.

889
01:17:48.131 --> 01:17:49.607
Some men.

890
01:17:50.769 --> 01:17:52.970
-Bandits.
-A man. bandits?

891
01:17:53.819 --> 01:17:55.758
-Yes.
-Huh. May I look?

892
01:17:59.742 --> 01:18:00.743
(ROBIN INHALES SHARPLY)

893
01:18:01.619 --> 01:18:03.472
It's quite a blow.

894
01:18:03.496 --> 01:18:06.975
Oh. you're lucky you survived.
You're a lucky boy.

895
01:18:06.999 --> 01:18:08.059
Yes.

896
01:18:08.083 --> 01:18:10.354
You should be thankful
to be alive.

897
01:18:10.378 --> 01:18:12.672
-Yes.
-He used a quarterstaff?

898
01:18:18.969 --> 01:18:20.322
Hmm.

899
01:18:20.346 --> 01:18:22.265
Lucky it didn't
take your head off.

900
01:18:25.560 --> 01:18:26.995
(ROBIN SIGHS)

901
01:18:27.019 --> 01:18:28.688
BOY: (IN DISTANCE) Randolph.

902
01:18:31.441 --> 01:18:32.692
Randolph.

903
01:18:35.583 --> 01:18:36.626
(SHOUTS) Moshe?

904
01:18:40.366 --> 01:18:43.077
The Prioress said to come.

905
01:18:43.786 --> 01:18:45.371
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

906
01:18:50.210 --> 01:18:52.378
(THE LEPER BREATHES WEAKLY)

907
01:19:19.697 --> 01:19:20.865
(WHEEZES)

908
01:19:24.619 --> 01:19:26.829
-Are you in great pain?
-(THE LEPER GROANS)

909
01:19:32.011 --> 01:19:33.305
(GROANS)

910
01:19:35.738 --> 01:19:37.952
Do you remember the trees?

911
01:19:40.369 --> 01:19:42.371
Pears. apples and elderberries.

912
01:19:44.823 --> 01:19:46.075
Wonderful.

913
01:19:48.014 --> 01:19:49.265
(BREATHING HOARSELY)

914
01:19:52.591 --> 01:19:53.843
(GROANS)

915
01:19:56.662 --> 01:19:59.849
You know that you are
the most important person

916
01:19:59.874 --> 01:20:01.668
in Little Margaret's life.

917
01:20:02.151 --> 01:20:05.112
Ah. I'm not important.

918
01:20:05.584 --> 01:20:06.585
(THE LEPER GROANS)

919
01:20:12.374 --> 01:20:13.374
(GROANS)

920
01:20:17.632 --> 01:20:19.029
Think of all the people

921
01:20:19.054 --> 01:20:20.973
whose lives you've crossed.

922
01:20:22.606 --> 01:20:24.334
(THE LEPER GROANS)

923
01:20:24.359 --> 01:20:27.153
We were important somehow
to all of them.

924
01:20:34.650 --> 01:20:37.778
Do you know the story
of Guy of Gisborne

925
01:20:39.774 --> 01:20:41.316
and Robin Hood?

926
01:20:46.484 --> 01:20:47.778
Yes.

927
01:20:52.683 --> 01:20:55.019
They say you killed him.

928
01:20:55.765 --> 01:20:56.909
(THE LEPER GROANS)

929
01:20:56.934 --> 01:20:58.453
Did you really behead him?

930
01:20:58.483 --> 01:21:01.862
-You are confused. leper.
-Well. I'll not tell a soul.

931
01:21:04.684 --> 01:21:07.687
But don't lie to a man
on his deathbed.

932
01:21:10.047 --> 01:21:13.633
So. did you really behead him?

933
01:21:17.234 --> 01:21:19.545
There were no Guy of Gisborne.

934
01:21:19.570 --> 01:21:22.656
It were just one of the many
tales that passed along.

935
01:21:24.959 --> 01:21:26.544
But I beheaded other men.

936
01:21:29.523 --> 01:21:31.296
(BREATHES HEAVILY)

937
01:21:34.387 --> 01:21:36.389
You really don't remember?

938
01:21:37.255 --> 01:21:38.483
(THE LEPER SCOFFS SOFTLY)

939
01:21:38.521 --> 01:21:40.790
No. (SNORTS. GULPS)

940
01:21:40.815 --> 01:21:42.777
Think about that name.

941
01:21:47.295 --> 01:21:49.673
There were a Guy of Gisborne.

942
01:21:51.167 --> 01:21:52.334
(THE LEPER SIGHS)

943
01:21:53.420 --> 01:21:55.130
But you did not behead him.

944
01:21:58.144 --> 01:21:59.562
You cut off his ear.

945
01:22:03.321 --> 01:22:05.282
(SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING)

946
01:22:07.302 --> 01:22:12.367
You said. in another life.
you'd share a drink with him.

947
01:22:12.425 --> 01:22:13.635
(WHEEZES)

948
01:22:14.674 --> 01:22:16.050
Do you remember that?

949
01:22:28.144 --> 01:22:31.355
We seem to have
found another life.

950
01:22:34.674 --> 01:22:35.883
(SIGHS)

951
01:22:38.253 --> 01:22:41.149
THE LEPER: Now.
there is one cruelty

952
01:22:41.174 --> 01:22:43.736
I would ask you
to not bring about.

953
01:22:43.761 --> 01:22:46.156
(WHEEZES)

954
01:22:46.181 --> 01:22:48.201
(BREATHING WEAKLY) You will
guard the orchard

955
01:22:48.226 --> 01:22:50.478
until you too die.

956
01:22:53.580 --> 01:22:55.832
You will serve the Prioress...

957
01:22:57.507 --> 01:23:01.136
and the people of this Priory.
past and future.

958
01:23:05.792 --> 01:23:09.504
But at no point in that time...

959
01:23:12.074 --> 01:23:16.711
in those
good and peaceful years.

960
01:23:19.534 --> 01:23:22.930
will you tell the Prioress
who you really are.

961
01:23:22.955 --> 01:23:24.098
(BREATHES HEAVILY)

962
01:23:24.123 --> 01:23:26.292
(SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES PLAYING)

963
01:23:29.261 --> 01:23:30.303
Why?

964
01:23:32.875 --> 01:23:34.126
Because...

965
01:23:36.074 --> 01:23:38.052
one of those nameless.

966
01:23:38.077 --> 01:23:39.345
faceless deaths

967
01:23:39.370 --> 01:23:41.414
in the shadows of your mind...

968
01:23:44.186 --> 01:23:45.938
were in another life...

969
01:23:48.775 --> 01:23:50.192
her beloved.

970
01:23:50.769 --> 01:23:52.939
(THE LEPER CONTINUES
BREATHING WEAKLY)

971
01:23:58.553 --> 01:23:59.595
Promise me.

972
01:24:04.839 --> 01:24:06.048
Robin...

973
01:24:07.893 --> 01:24:09.144
Promise me.

974
01:24:14.162 --> 01:24:16.373
(TENDER MUSIC PLAYING)

975
01:24:36.560 --> 01:24:44.084
WOMAN: ♪ Sumer is icumen in
Loude sing cuccu! ♪

976
01:24:44.109 --> 01:24:47.297
♪ Groweth seed
and bloweth meed ♪

977
01:24:47.322 --> 01:24:50.968
♪ And springth the wode now ♪

978
01:24:50.993 --> 01:24:54.598
♪ Sing cuccu ♪

979
01:24:54.623 --> 01:25:01.064
♪ Ewe bleteth after lamb
Loweth after calve cow ♪

980
01:25:01.089 --> 01:25:04.902
♪ Bulloc sterteth
bucke verteth ♪

981
01:25:04.927 --> 01:25:07.781
♪ Merye sing cuccu! ♪

982
01:25:07.806 --> 01:25:14.372
♪ Cuccu. cuccu
Wel singest thou cuccu! ♪

983
01:25:14.397 --> 01:25:16.417
♪ Ne swik thou never now! ♪

984
01:25:16.442 --> 01:25:18.652
-(SONG FADES)
-(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

985
01:25:24.563 --> 01:25:26.523
(SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING)

986
01:25:35.966 --> 01:25:37.718
(FOOTSTEPS RECEDING)

987
01:25:40.869 --> 01:25:42.519
ROBIN: (WHISPERS)
Good-bye. Brigid.

988
01:25:52.687 --> 01:25:53.813
(FIRE CRACKLES)

989
01:25:55.773 --> 01:25:56.941
ROBIN: Arthur.

990
01:25:59.232 --> 01:26:00.316
Come.

991
01:26:01.481 --> 01:26:03.542
(BOAT CREAKING)

992
01:26:03.567 --> 01:26:05.707
There's a child
on the far shore.

993
01:26:07.033 --> 01:26:08.409
Perhaps it's your niece.

994
01:26:10.600 --> 01:26:12.727
The Leper said
you sought your lost niece.

995
01:26:14.348 --> 01:26:15.740
Yes.

996
01:26:15.947 --> 01:26:18.954
-Could it be her?
-We shall see.

997
01:26:20.891 --> 01:26:23.059
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

998
01:26:57.828 --> 01:26:59.830
I do not see signs of anyone.

999
01:27:01.207 --> 01:27:02.541
Ah. we should wait.

1000
01:27:03.482 --> 01:27:04.900
Maybe they will return.

1001
01:27:27.057 --> 01:27:28.308
What is your name?

1002
01:27:32.493 --> 01:27:33.577
Arthur.

1003
01:27:34.752 --> 01:27:36.855
Do not waste time lying to me.

1004
01:27:36.879 --> 01:27:38.130
What is your real name?

1005
01:27:39.882 --> 01:27:41.508
(BREATH TREMBLES)

1006
01:27:43.094 --> 01:27:44.178
Godwyn.

1007
01:27:47.473 --> 01:27:49.868
You are deciding. Godwyn.

1008
01:27:49.892 --> 01:27:52.061
whether to do
the deed yourself...

1009
01:27:53.354 --> 01:27:54.856
or to fetch your family.

1010
01:27:58.275 --> 01:27:59.211
What deed?

1011
01:27:59.235 --> 01:28:01.403
How many men
have you killed. Godwyn?

1012
01:28:02.905 --> 01:28:05.633
How many children
have you killed?

1013
01:28:05.657 --> 01:28:07.869
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1014
01:28:11.038 --> 01:28:14.125
I have killed so many.
I could not give you a count.

1015
01:28:15.877 --> 01:28:17.730
For longer than
you've been alive.

1016
01:28:17.754 --> 01:28:20.733
I've been killing the kin of
those I killed a lifetime ago.

1017
01:28:20.757 --> 01:28:22.776
I do not remember the first.

1018
01:28:22.800 --> 01:28:25.094
who meant nothing to me
at the time. but...

1019
01:28:26.345 --> 01:28:28.365
their brothers
and their children.

1020
01:28:28.389 --> 01:28:31.017
their grandchildren.
they remember me.

1021
01:28:31.976 --> 01:28:34.020
So now I must kill them.

1022
01:28:34.979 --> 01:28:37.499
Again and again.

1023
01:28:37.523 --> 01:28:41.527
In different forms.
like shades. Again.

1024
01:28:42.904 --> 01:28:45.072
And again. and it never ceases.

1025
01:28:48.700 --> 01:28:50.411
It's a curse. Godwyn.

1026
01:28:52.246 --> 01:28:53.891
And it's one
you bring on yourself.

1027
01:28:53.915 --> 01:28:56.625
even if done through duty.

1028
01:28:57.626 --> 01:28:59.628
It cares not about your duty.

1029
01:29:00.421 --> 01:29:03.424
This world cares
only about blood.

1030
01:29:05.176 --> 01:29:07.386
And blood is all
it will give in return.

1031
01:29:10.097 --> 01:29:13.059
But do you want
to kill a child. Godwyn?

1032
01:29:15.352 --> 01:29:16.955
Do you want to be responsible

1033
01:29:16.979 --> 01:29:19.398
for the killing
of a little girl?

1034
01:29:20.357 --> 01:29:21.400
(SNIFFLES)

1035
01:29:22.819 --> 01:29:24.028
(VOICE BREAKING) No.

1036
01:29:35.873 --> 01:29:37.374
Your father's dead?

1037
01:29:38.960 --> 01:29:40.020
And your uncles?

1038
01:29:40.044 --> 01:29:41.253
(SNIFFLES)

1039
01:29:43.146 --> 01:29:44.898
I am the eldest left.

1040
01:29:46.425 --> 01:29:47.426
(SIGHS)

1041
01:29:49.516 --> 01:29:50.893
Who else yet lives. Godwyn?

1042
01:29:53.417 --> 01:29:54.501
My mother.

1043
01:29:56.101 --> 01:29:57.144
My aunts.

1044
01:29:58.980 --> 01:30:00.582
My sisters.

1045
01:30:00.606 --> 01:30:02.524
You have a home. Godwyn?

1046
01:30:04.701 --> 01:30:06.452
-Yes.
-Go home.

1047
01:30:07.947 --> 01:30:10.574
Tell your family
all blood debts are paid.

1048
01:30:11.283 --> 01:30:13.077
They'll all be paid someday.

1049
01:30:15.287 --> 01:30:16.622
Sleep in your own bed.

1050
01:30:17.735 --> 01:30:19.880
Hold dear the life

1051
01:30:19.905 --> 01:30:22.032
you will yet share
with your kin.

1052
01:30:23.715 --> 01:30:25.425
And if you return here.

1053
01:30:26.491 --> 01:30:28.052
you will have wasted this chance

1054
01:30:28.077 --> 01:30:29.996
at life that I give you now.

1055
01:30:31.802 --> 01:30:33.655
And I will cut your throat

1056
01:30:33.680 --> 01:30:35.431
and never think of you again.

1057
01:30:42.105 --> 01:30:43.148
Go now.

1058
01:30:45.778 --> 01:30:47.071
And do not look back.

1059
01:31:00.855 --> 01:31:02.565
(SIGHS HEAVILY)

1060
01:31:20.813 --> 01:31:22.982
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

1061
01:31:41.678 --> 01:31:43.948
I thought
you had departed. (SOBS)

1062
01:31:43.973 --> 01:31:45.975
(BREATHES HEAVILY)

1063
01:31:53.404 --> 01:31:54.905
I am Robin the Outlaw.

1064
01:31:58.904 --> 01:32:02.574
You... You need to know
that I'm a monster.

1065
01:32:04.877 --> 01:32:06.336
I'm not one Randolph.

1066
01:32:09.169 --> 01:32:12.422
I am the outlaw. Robin Hood.

1067
01:32:14.102 --> 01:32:16.270
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1068
01:32:22.500 --> 01:32:24.461
(SOBBING BREATHS)

1069
01:32:27.247 --> 01:32:29.416
(MUMBLES) I'm sorry...

1070
01:32:33.112 --> 01:32:35.281
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1071
01:32:42.683 --> 01:32:43.934
(GRUNTS)

1072
01:32:55.159 --> 01:32:56.511
(FIRE CRACKLES)

1073
01:32:56.536 --> 01:32:58.789
(DRAMATIC MUSIC
CONTINUES PLAYING)

1074
01:33:12.012 --> 01:33:13.222
(WILD BOAR GRUNTS)

1075
01:33:14.723 --> 01:33:16.892
(BOWSTRING STRETCHING)

1076
01:33:31.370 --> 01:33:32.222
(ARROW THUDS)

1077
01:33:32.247 --> 01:33:34.416
(WILD BOAR'S BODY DRAGGING)

1078
01:33:51.597 --> 01:33:52.597
(GROANS)

1079
01:33:57.846 --> 01:34:00.015
(DRAMATIC MUSIC
CONTINUES PLAYING)

1080
01:34:06.696 --> 01:34:07.738
(MUSIC FADES)

1081
01:34:09.180 --> 01:34:11.182
(PANTING)

1082
01:34:29.234 --> 01:34:30.915
Tell me I should leave.

1083
01:34:33.350 --> 01:34:34.912
I will go now.

1084
01:34:42.733 --> 01:34:44.026
Get in the bed.

1085
01:35:04.004 --> 01:35:05.714
-Brigid...
-Lie down.

1086
01:35:32.137 --> 01:35:33.137
(BOWL CLATTERS)

1087
01:35:46.070 --> 01:35:48.156
(ROBIN SIGHS)

1088
01:35:50.951 --> 01:35:52.786
(BREATHING DEEPLY)

1089
01:35:57.789 --> 01:35:59.959
(BLOOD CONTINUES DRIPPING)

1090
01:36:16.083 --> 01:36:18.252
(TRAGIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1091
01:36:29.567 --> 01:36:31.736
(BREATHING SLOWS)

1092
01:37:03.848 --> 01:37:05.016
(SIGHS SOFTLY)

1093
01:37:08.668 --> 01:37:10.003
(SIGHS)

1094
01:37:12.993 --> 01:37:15.203
(TRAGIC MUSIC CONTINUES PLAYING)

1095
01:37:19.961 --> 01:37:21.171
(DOOR CLOSES)

1096
01:37:34.763 --> 01:37:36.240
(LAUGHS)

1097
01:37:36.265 --> 01:37:38.434
(DISTURBING MUSIC PLAYING)

1098
01:37:40.468 --> 01:37:42.637
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

1099
01:38:31.169 --> 01:38:33.421
You burned my husband alive.

1100
01:38:38.867 --> 01:38:40.596
I dream that
he was already dead.

1101
01:38:40.621 --> 01:38:43.374
but why else did you bar
the door? (SOBS)

1102
01:38:47.565 --> 01:38:49.427
It felt like a lifetime

1103
01:38:49.452 --> 01:38:51.997
searching the ashes of our home.

1104
01:38:54.853 --> 01:38:56.776
And he looked so small.

1105
01:38:58.718 --> 01:39:02.555
Curled up in the corner
with so much of him gone.

1106
01:39:07.059 --> 01:39:08.332
But as much as I dream.

1107
01:39:08.357 --> 01:39:09.858
I know he was alive.

1108
01:39:14.864 --> 01:39:16.675
Because. until the very end.

1109
01:39:16.700 --> 01:39:18.135
he had wrapped himself

1110
01:39:18.160 --> 01:39:20.204
around our children.

1111
01:39:27.971 --> 01:39:29.680
(EXHALES)

1112
01:39:30.192 --> 01:39:32.402
(TRAGIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1113
01:39:53.770 --> 01:39:55.730
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

1114
01:39:58.230 --> 01:39:59.690
(DOOR CLOSES)

1115
01:40:01.578 --> 01:40:02.996
(KNOCK ON DOOR)

1116
01:40:03.610 --> 01:40:05.069
(DOOR RATTLES)

1117
01:40:07.718 --> 01:40:09.636
-LITTLE MARGARET: Randolph...
-(GASPS SOFTLY)

1118
01:40:11.561 --> 01:40:12.812
It's me.

1119
01:40:14.938 --> 01:40:16.339
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1120
01:40:16.364 --> 01:40:18.802
(FOOTSTEPS RECEDING)

1121
01:40:19.299 --> 01:40:21.342
(SOBBING SOFTLY)

1122
01:40:30.912 --> 01:40:33.122
(SISTER BRIGID SOBBING)

1123
01:40:55.637 --> 01:40:57.764
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

1124
01:41:06.912 --> 01:41:09.080
ROBIN: People speak
of Robin Hood.

1125
01:41:11.003 --> 01:41:12.170
(ROBIN SIGHS)

1126
01:41:14.151 --> 01:41:15.736
Tell his stories.

1127
01:41:21.970 --> 01:41:23.514
They're all lies.

1128
01:41:27.211 --> 01:41:29.922
Lies that I told long ago.

1129
01:41:32.010 --> 01:41:33.849
So that fools would...

1130
01:41:35.251 --> 01:41:37.336
follow me into the dark.

1131
01:41:39.215 --> 01:41:41.425
(BREATHING WEAKLY)

1132
01:41:46.595 --> 01:41:49.348
EDWARD: Robin. (ECHOING)

1133
01:41:54.219 --> 01:41:56.137
What have they done to you?

1134
01:42:01.853 --> 01:42:03.730
EDWARD: Don't be afraid.

1135
01:42:05.886 --> 01:42:08.556
I will rescue you
from this place.

1136
01:42:10.567 --> 01:42:12.861
I'll rescue Little Margaret.

1137
01:42:14.492 --> 01:42:17.661
And we're gonna start
a new life together.

1138
01:42:18.371 --> 01:42:19.413
Edward...

1139
01:42:23.672 --> 01:42:25.883
tell me about your wife.

1140
01:42:29.882 --> 01:42:32.092
(ROBIN BREATHING WEAKLY)

1141
01:42:35.669 --> 01:42:36.878
My wife.

1142
01:42:39.673 --> 01:42:40.882
ROBIN: Margaret.

1143
01:42:45.105 --> 01:42:46.315
(SOFTLY) Margaret.

1144
01:42:48.692 --> 01:42:50.611
My wife. Margaret.

1145
01:42:52.905 --> 01:42:54.490
Paint a portrait.

1146
01:42:57.075 --> 01:42:58.452
EDWARD: Paint a portrait?

1147
01:43:02.813 --> 01:43:04.232
She has hair...

1148
01:43:06.377 --> 01:43:07.503
red like...

1149
01:43:09.423 --> 01:43:11.300
the setting sun.

1150
01:43:14.177 --> 01:43:17.430
Like the setting summer sun.

1151
01:43:24.561 --> 01:43:25.562
Red like...

1152
01:43:26.371 --> 01:43:28.540
the setting summer...

1153
01:43:29.751 --> 01:43:31.045
sun.

1154
01:43:33.649 --> 01:43:34.834
(GASPS)

1155
01:43:34.859 --> 01:43:36.694
(INDISTINCT VOICES WHISPERING)

1156
01:43:49.111 --> 01:43:50.112
Robin...

1157
01:43:56.375 --> 01:43:58.668
Have you found your right death?

1158
01:44:04.206 --> 01:44:06.291
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

1159
01:44:31.963 --> 01:44:34.131
(LIMPING FOOTSTEPS APPROACH)

1160
01:44:44.475 --> 01:44:45.475
(GRUNTS)

1161
01:44:46.227 --> 01:44:48.437
(PANTING)

1162
01:44:59.334 --> 01:45:01.378
(SOFTLY) I'm ready to finish it.

1163
01:45:08.445 --> 01:45:10.197
I owe this life to you.

1164
01:45:18.117 --> 01:45:19.618
(WHISPERING) It is monstrous.

1165
01:45:24.190 --> 01:45:26.192
But I owe this life to you.

1166
01:45:26.820 --> 01:45:28.406
You owe me nothing.

1167
01:45:33.581 --> 01:45:35.875
I have never taken
a life before.

1168
01:45:37.676 --> 01:45:38.677
Ah.

1169
01:45:40.382 --> 01:45:43.052
It can be
as if pruning a flower.

1170
01:45:45.070 --> 01:45:46.797
Well. it should not be.

1171
01:45:46.822 --> 01:45:49.159
Aye. it should not.

1172
01:45:50.471 --> 01:45:51.597
But it can.

1173
01:45:57.641 --> 01:46:00.269
I help those
who come to this island.

1174
01:46:03.050 --> 01:46:04.301
I heal them.

1175
01:46:08.151 --> 01:46:09.194
Please.

1176
01:46:14.772 --> 01:46:16.189
Heal me.

1177
01:46:20.872 --> 01:46:23.083
(SERENE MUSIC PLAYING)

1178
01:47:11.874 --> 01:47:13.416
Little Margaret...

1179
01:47:19.074 --> 01:47:21.368
your father's name were John.

1180
01:47:30.837 --> 01:47:32.964
I knew him for many years.

1181
01:47:34.338 --> 01:47:36.506
Before he were your papa.

1182
01:47:38.971 --> 01:47:40.222
(GRUNTS WEAKLY)

1183
01:47:42.312 --> 01:47:43.439
I met him...

1184
01:47:45.091 --> 01:47:47.177
crossing a bridge one day...

1185
01:47:48.756 --> 01:47:51.008
over a rushing river.

1186
01:47:53.606 --> 01:47:55.065
He was stubborn.

1187
01:47:58.024 --> 01:48:00.419
He would not yield.

1188
01:48:00.444 --> 01:48:03.572
Oh. not to any man.

1189
01:48:05.071 --> 01:48:06.490
Not even to me.

1190
01:48:10.005 --> 01:48:11.506
So we wrestled.

1191
01:48:12.377 --> 01:48:13.804
On that bridge.

1192
01:48:15.724 --> 01:48:18.935
Striking. Back and forth.

1193
01:48:20.878 --> 01:48:23.632
I whacked him
on the side of the head.

1194
01:48:25.929 --> 01:48:28.098
He struck me in the stomach.

1195
01:48:29.554 --> 01:48:31.847
And I wobbled on that bridge.

1196
01:48:33.685 --> 01:48:34.936
Splash!

1197
01:48:36.227 --> 01:48:38.439
-He knocked me on me bum.
-(CHUCKLES)

1198
01:48:42.398 --> 01:48:44.526
Once I dragged myself out.

1199
01:48:45.432 --> 01:48:47.016
drenched to the bone.

1200
01:48:48.823 --> 01:48:50.032
we embraced.

1201
01:48:53.704 --> 01:48:55.288
We called your papa...

1202
01:48:56.251 --> 01:48:57.555
Little John.

1203
01:48:59.106 --> 01:49:01.275
And we lived for many years...

1204
01:49:04.421 --> 01:49:07.882
as outlaws in the greenwood.

1205
01:49:10.963 --> 01:49:12.780
Oh. we had feasts.

1206
01:49:13.841 --> 01:49:14.842
We...

1207
01:49:15.698 --> 01:49:17.116
We gave silver...

1208
01:49:18.100 --> 01:49:19.407
to the meek.

1209
01:49:23.983 --> 01:49:25.526
(SOFTLY) No...

1210
01:49:36.524 --> 01:49:38.818
But we stole that silver.

1211
01:49:44.721 --> 01:49:45.972
We stole it...

1212
01:49:47.353 --> 01:49:50.648
from. from bad people.

1213
01:49:55.571 --> 01:49:56.822
(SOFTLY) You understand?

1214
01:49:59.489 --> 01:50:00.532
Bad people.

1215
01:50:10.017 --> 01:50:12.019
(BREATHING WEAKLY)

1216
01:50:15.876 --> 01:50:17.128
Your papa...

1217
01:50:18.616 --> 01:50:20.368
would want me to tell you...

1218
01:50:26.594 --> 01:50:29.347
because he loved you so dearly.

1219
01:50:32.853 --> 01:50:35.315
You must never tell a soul.

1220
01:50:36.937 --> 01:50:39.315
Not even the children
you play with.

1221
01:50:40.850 --> 01:50:44.479
You must never tell them
your papa's name.

1222
01:50:48.899 --> 01:50:50.984
There are bad people out there.

1223
01:50:53.708 --> 01:50:57.378
And they are angry
with your papa.

1224
01:50:58.918 --> 01:51:00.085
(ROBIN SIGHS)

1225
01:51:01.744 --> 01:51:03.806
(SOFTLY)
And so they're angry with you.

1226
01:51:03.831 --> 01:51:05.166
(SOBBING QUIETLY)

1227
01:51:08.782 --> 01:51:11.160
And can we keep that secret?

1228
01:51:13.495 --> 01:51:16.290
I can keep that secret.
Little Margaret.

1229
01:51:18.698 --> 01:51:19.949
Can you?

1230
01:51:24.424 --> 01:51:25.968
ROBIN: Good.

1231
01:51:27.986 --> 01:51:29.787
Now come beside me.

1232
01:51:32.615 --> 01:51:33.825
(SNIFFLES)

1233
01:51:39.654 --> 01:51:40.905
Take this.

1234
01:51:42.863 --> 01:51:44.199
Why were he "Little"?

1235
01:51:45.203 --> 01:51:46.204
What?

1236
01:51:47.458 --> 01:51:49.603
Why were my papa
called "Little"?

1237
01:51:49.628 --> 01:51:51.839
(ROBIN BREATHING SHALLOW)

1238
01:51:55.316 --> 01:51:57.902
Because he were little
when I found him.

1239
01:51:59.682 --> 01:52:00.784
Like you.

1240
01:52:00.809 --> 01:52:02.979
(TENDER MUSIC PLAYING)

1241
01:52:08.948 --> 01:52:10.199
String it.

1242
01:52:33.450 --> 01:52:36.620
Bend it with your leg
as you saw me do.

1243
01:52:44.935 --> 01:52:46.269
(BOW CREAKS)

1244
01:52:53.112 --> 01:52:54.113
(SOFTLY) Good.

1245
01:52:56.122 --> 01:52:59.875
Now. go to the window.

1246
01:53:08.190 --> 01:53:10.067
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1247
01:53:16.727 --> 01:53:18.896
(TENDER MUSIC CONTINUES)

1248
01:53:20.149 --> 01:53:21.192
Now.

1249
01:53:23.309 --> 01:53:24.605
nock an arrow.

1250
01:53:33.456 --> 01:53:34.891
Find a point

1251
01:53:35.909 --> 01:53:38.286
where the waters meet the sky.

1252
01:53:43.413 --> 01:53:45.665
Pull that arrow to your mouth.

1253
01:53:49.633 --> 01:53:50.927
And hold.

1254
01:53:52.749 --> 01:53:54.876
I will tell you when to loose.

1255
01:53:57.779 --> 01:53:59.197
And when I do...

1256
01:54:00.271 --> 01:54:01.773
you're not letting go.

1257
01:54:04.797 --> 01:54:07.497
You're simply
not holding on anymore.

1258
01:54:12.087 --> 01:54:13.088
Now.

1259
01:54:14.625 --> 01:54:16.126
Watch that target.

1260
01:54:19.488 --> 01:54:22.033
Your body will always be moving.

1261
01:54:25.050 --> 01:54:29.554
Feel when that arrow
will fly true.

1262
01:54:32.625 --> 01:54:34.835
You're gonna find a dance.

1263
01:54:37.144 --> 01:54:39.647
Hold until I tell you to loose.

1264
01:54:43.360 --> 01:54:44.987
You are strong.

1265
01:54:45.966 --> 01:54:47.550
Feel...

1266
01:54:49.331 --> 01:54:50.817
that sway.

1267
01:54:54.067 --> 01:54:55.428
that dance.

1268
01:55:00.708 --> 01:55:01.935
(MUSIC FADES)

1269
01:55:02.453 --> 01:55:03.931
Now loose.

1270
01:55:03.956 --> 01:55:07.167
-(ARROW FIRES)
-(WAVES CRASHING)

1271
01:55:17.332 --> 01:55:19.334
(TENDER MUSIC RESUMES)

1272
01:56:54.921 --> 01:56:57.090
(SOLEMN MUSIC PLAYING)

1273
02:01:43.900 --> 02:01:45.256
(MUSIC FADES)

1273
02:01:46.305 --> 02:02:46.205
